        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "82bf04e0-143d-5ce8-92d4-647d2d260bb4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mary Tarrero-Serrano, Carlos Prío Socarrás, Fulgencio Batista, Osvaldo Farrés, Antonio Prío Socarrás\n- Roles: Cuban President, Cuban First Lady, Minister of Housing, banker\n- Events: military coup in Cuba, Cuban Revolution\n- Works: \"Quizás, Quizás, Quizás\"\n\nFacts:\n- Fulgencio Batista was the elected President of Cuba from 1940 to 1944.\n- Carlos Prío Socarrás was the President of Cuba during 1948 to 1952.\n- Antonio Prío Socarrás was a Cuban banker and served as Minister of Housing from 1948 to 1950 during the presidency of his brother, Carlos Prío Socarrás.\n- Mary Tarrero-Serrano was the second wife of Cuban President Carlos Prío Socarrás.\n- Mary Tarrero-Serrano was Cuban First Lady.\n- Osvaldo Farrés received help and inspiration for the lyrics of \"Quizás, Quizás, Quizás\" from Mary Tarrero-Serrano.\n- Fulgencio Batista overthrew Carlos Prío Socarrás in a military coup in 1952.\n- Fulgencio Batista was a U.S.-backed dictator of Cuba from 1952 to 1959.\n- Fulgencio Batista was overthrown during the Cuban Revolution.\n- Fulgencio Batista was born as Rubén Zaldívar on January 16, 1901, and died on August 6, 1973.\n- Antonio Prío Socarrás was born in Cuba on June 29, 1905, and died in Miami, Florida, on September 6, 1990.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "bfc725c1-c11a-5783-97a1-d4a22dc9f83a",
        "text": "Page: Mary Tarrero-Serrano. Sentence: She was the second wife of Cuban President, Carlos Prio, who was overthrown by Fulgencio Batista in a military coup.\nPage: Fulgencio Batista. Sentence: Fulgencio Batista y Zaldívar (] ; born Rubén Zaldívar; January 16, 1901 – August 6, 1973) was the elected President of Cuba from 1940 to 1944, and U.S.-backed dictator from 1952 to 1959, before being overthrown during the Cuban Revolution.\nPage: Quizás, Quizás, Quizás. Sentence: Farrés also received much help and inspiration for his lyrics from Cuban First Lady, Mary Tarrero-Serrano.\nPage: Antonio Prío. Sentence: Antonio Prío Socarrás (June 29, 1905 in Cuba - September 6, 1990 in Miami, Florida USA) was a Cuban banker and Minister of Housing (1948-1950) during the presidency of his brother Cuban President, Carlos Prío Socarrás.",
